Package: bogentag
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/excelano/bogentag-desktop
Depends: libc6, libgcc-s1, libwayland-client0, libxkbcommon0, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libegl1, libvulkan1 | libgl1, libx11-6, libx11-xcb1, libxi6, libxcursor1, libxrandr2, desktop-file-utils, hicolor-icon-theme
Description: The time read from the Sun's arc
 Bogentag shows the time as Bogenzeit: where the Sun is on its arc for the
 day, in spans before or after solar noon or solar midnight where you are,
 or in kiloseconds from them. The dial is a sky with its twilight bands and
 the Sun on its track; a click on it shows UTC and the local clock.
 .
 It has a day page with the lengths of the day and night arcs and the times
 of sunrise, solar noon, sunset and solar midnight, a timer and a stopwatch
 that count in spans or kiloseconds, and an explainer of the standard.
 Everything is computed on this computer; it makes no network connection.
